(958124, 109200, 12962, '<td valign="top">This is so well done.  Very professionally finished.  Congratulations!</td>', 'This is so well done.  Very professionally finished.  Congratulations!', '2004-10-13 16:49:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(958138, 109228, 8054, '<td valign="top">From a technical standpoint, I see these flaws: contrast, lighting and cropping. Contrast and lighting are flawed in a similar way. The low light levels affects the overall contrast of this image. Like you mentioned yourself, it needs to be cropped to get rid of that white spot.<br/> <br/>Aesthetically, it just doesn''t pack a visual punch. I see the railing, the water, bits of the roof and the sunset but there isn''t a main focal point that grabs my attention.<br/> <br/>Hope that helps! By the way, I did not vote in this challenge.</td>', 'From a technical standpoint, I see these flaws: contrast, lighting and cropping. Contrast and lighting are flawed in a similar way. The low light levels affects the overall contrast of this image. Like you mentioned yourself, it needs to be cropped to get rid of that white spot. Aesthetically, it just doesn''t pack a visual punch. I see the railing, the water, bits of the roof and the sunset but there isn''t a main focal point that grabs my attention. Hope that helps! By the way, I did not vote in this challenge.', '2004-10-13 16:56:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(958192, 109200, 5746, '<td valign="top">Congratulations!<br/>One of my favourites</td>', 'Congratulations!One of my favourites', '2004-10-13 17:46:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(958244, 109394, 5746, '<td valign="top">It should be top 5 :)<br/>Great job!<br/></td>', 'It should be top 5 :)Great job!', '2004-10-13 18:37:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(958291, 110454, 12611, '<td valign="top">Thanks for all your great comments. This shot was taken in a fishing boat at about 6 am going through the jamestown bridge in narragansett bay. The pillar on the left is the new bridge, the one on the right is the old bridge. I have several outakes which I may post in my portfolio and some different shots on the water for the october free study. <br/> <br/>I was really lucky to be there at this time and the mist was really amazing. We were riding in the boat with radar and you could see the daybreak straight up, but only about 35 yards out in front of the boat. crazy really.  <br/> <br/> I used no-flash auto iso so that I would a clear shot- but it was a bit too grainy. All I did was hit "auto levels" and I really liked what it did. And then I resized. Thats it. <br/> <br/>Thanks again.</td>', 'Thanks for all your great comments. This shot was taken in a fishing boat at about 6 am going through the jamestown bridge in narragansett bay. The pillar on the left is the new bridge, the one on the right is the old bridge. I have several outakes which I may post in my portfolio and some different shots on the water for the october free study.  I was really lucky to be there at this time and the mist was really amazing. We were riding in the boat with radar and you could see the daybreak straight up, but only about 35 yards out in front of the boat. crazy really.    I used no-flash auto iso so that I would a clear shot- but it was a bit too grainy. All I did was hit "auto levels" and I really liked what it did. And then I resized. Thats it.  Thanks again.', '2004-10-13 19:18:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(958312, 109394, 9763, '<td valign="top">Wow Kylie!  I am soooooo proud of you!  You have surpassed me a million times over.  You are such a great motivator and friend on DPC.  Congrats on your great entry!</td>', 'Wow Kylie!  I am soooooo proud of you!  You have surpassed me a million times over.  You are such a great motivator and friend on DPC.  Congrats on your great entry!', '2004-10-13 19:34:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(958431, 110027, 18191, '<td valign="top">Thanks Sonja and everyone else for your helpful comments...I had a blast with this image---4th best, woohoo!</td>', 'Thanks Sonja and everyone else for your helpful comments...I had a blast with this image---4th best, woohoo!', '2004-10-13 20:32:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(958464, 110521, 26401, '<td valign="top">My intent was to have the cartridge and in particular the stylus tip in perfect focus with some of the surrounding groves.<br/> <br/>Lighting was a problem. All I had was a couple of halogens on the ceiling and a friend holding a flashlight.<br/> <br/>I tried to hand hold the shot but could not get the focus right. I finally used a tripod but it was very difficult to position and I didn''t want to move the turntable and have to go through the setup again.<br/> <br/>I did want a shallow depth of field but a bit stronger light would have allowed me to stop down a bit and make the back of the tone arm a bit more distinct.<br/> <br/>This was my first contest attempt after having the camera for 2 days. I appreciate all of your comments.</td>', 'My intent was to have the cartridge and in particular the stylus tip in perfect focus with some of the surrounding groves. Lighting was a problem. All I had was a couple of halogens on the ceiling and a friend holding a flashlight. I tried to hand hold the shot but could not get the focus right. I finally used a tripod but it was very difficult to position and I didn''t want to move the turntable and have to go through the setup again. I did want a shallow depth of field but a bit stronger light would have allowed me to stop down a bit and make the back of the tone arm a bit more distinct. This was my first contest attempt after having the camera for 2 days. I appreciate all of your comments.', '2004-10-13 20:56:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(958549, 110095, 8367, '<td valign="top">Very nice detail and clarity. I''d love to see more of this building. It looks charming.<br/>Just read this again and thought I''d clarify.<br/>I''d love to see more of this building = I hope you post additional photos of this charming building. <br/>I love your crop on this one. :-D<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-11-30 15:12:14.</i></td>', 'Very nice detail and clarity. I''d love to see more of this building. It looks charming.Just read this again and thought I''d clarify.I''d love to see more of this building = I hope you post additional photos of this charming building. I love your crop on this one. :-D', '2004-10-13 21:29:26.000000', '2004-11-30 15:12:14.000000', 0),
