(960031, 108792, 15231, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by kdkaboom:</b></div><hr/><i> Honestly, I am so shocked this didn''t place higher. It''s really a great shot, and one of those three tens is from me. Congrats on the great shot! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks! It''s a bit of a visual pun, which people can interpret differently, so not surprising it did not score higher.  Still it''s my best yet (of 3 entries).  And since my last got 3%, I can''t complain.</td>', 'Originally posted by kdkaboom: Honestly, I am so shocked this didn''t place higher. It''s really a great shot, and one of those three tens is from me. Congrats on the great shot!   Thanks! It''s a bit of a visual pun, which people can interpret differently, so not surprising it did not score higher.  Still it''s my best yet (of 3 entries).  And since my last got 3%, I can''t complain.', '2004-10-14 22:13:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(960271, 110171, 8891, '<td valign="top">I agree...definitely should have been right up there. One of my favorites in the challenge.</td>', 'I agree...definitely should have been right up there. One of my favorites in the challenge.', '2004-10-15 01:50:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(960303, 108718, 27626, '<td valign="top">I think this should have done better.</td>', 'I think this should have done better.', '2004-10-15 02:49:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(960443, 109854, 27819, '<td valign="top">Well done Dan. Deserved top ten</td>', 'Well done Dan. Deserved top ten', '2004-10-15 07:26:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(961037, 110002, 9292, '<td valign="top">Thanks a lot for all your comments and votes. The next time I promise to clean all those little fuzzies ;-)</td>', 'Thanks a lot for all your comments and votes. The next time I promise to clean all those little fuzzies ;-)', '2004-10-15 19:21:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(961106, 109906, 7252, '<td valign="top">Oh yeah, you gotta love pumpkins. Brilliant orange globs of fall glory... ya just can''t be sad looking at pumpkins. Thank you for commenting. :)</td>', 'Oh yeah, you gotta love pumpkins. Brilliant orange globs of fall glory... ya just can''t be sad looking at pumpkins. Thank you for commenting. :)', '2004-10-15 20:21:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(961360, 109750, 2333, '<td valign="top">I am surprised this scored as low as it did. It''s techically well executed, and certainly meets the challenge. I did not vote this challenge, but would have given you a 6.<br/>That said, it just seems to lack the impact to take it to a higher score. What is the photo trying to say to the viewer? It seems to be a rather flat depiction of... parts. The diffuse lighting and relatively static composition combine to leave an impression of "nothing happening here."<br/>I also fall into this trap of having a well-executed photo, but missing any emotional message.</td>', 'I am surprised this scored as low as it did. It''s techically well executed, and certainly meets the challenge. I did not vote this challenge, but would have given you a 6.That said, it just seems to lack the impact to take it to a higher score. What is the photo trying to say to the viewer? It seems to be a rather flat depiction of... parts. The diffuse lighting and relatively static composition combine to leave an impression of "nothing happening here."I also fall into this trap of having a well-executed photo, but missing any emotional message.', '2004-10-16 00:51:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(961376, 110002, 20874, '<td valign="top">What makes this so great is seeing an incredibly common subject transformed into a treatise on composition, color, shadows, geometry and light largely just by looking closer.<br/> <br/>Bravo.</td>', 'What makes this so great is seeing an incredibly common subject transformed into a treatise on composition, color, shadows, geometry and light largely just by looking closer. Bravo.', '2004-10-16 01:13:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(961525, 109381, 24613, '<td valign="top">I didn''t vote on this challenge, but I like this shot alot.  I love the way the thread is out of focus and the focus on the needle area of the machine is really good!  Great job!  Looking forward to seeing more of your photography in the near future.</td>', 'I didn''t vote on this challenge, but I like this shot alot.  I love the way the thread is out of focus and the focus on the needle area of the machine is really good!  Great job!  Looking forward to seeing more of your photography in the near future.', '2004-10-16 09:18:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(961532, 109381, 26246, '<td valign="top">Really nice shot.</td>', 'Really nice shot.', '2004-10-16 09:38:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(961712, 109854, 12962, '<td valign="top">This is an incredible shot.  Very strong graphic design elements.  First submission, top ten!  I predict ribbons before too long.  Goes straight to my favorites.</td>', 'This is an incredible shot.  Very strong graphic design elements.  First submission, top ten!  I predict ribbons before too long.  Goes straight to my favorites.', '2004-10-16 13:05:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(961887, 110364, 27679, '<td valign="top"><b>Lessons learned:</b> <br/> <br/>* Do not start taking the photograph (or start using Photoshop) just a few hours before the competition closes. <br/>* Do not use your (clean) desk to place the subject on. Rather place it on a ''cleaner'' surface, e.g. a sheet of paper. This will hopefully eliminate dust problems, and yellow shadows.<br/>* Send it to DPC as the biggest 150 Kbyte JPEG file you can, not as a 60 Kbyte file. They <b>re-compress the image</b>, e.g. causing the texture of the cap to look like dust. Especially the thumbnail looks bad.<br/>* Watch the reflections e.g. in the bottle. Try maybe another sheet of paper.<br/>* Check the shadows under the bottle to get the shadow''s curve looking right.<br/>* Watch out for printed letters e.g. on the cap or the bottle.<br/></td>', 'Lessons learned:  * Do not start taking the photograph (or start using Photoshop) just a few hours before the competition closes. * Do not use your (clean) desk to place the subject on. Rather place it on a ''cleaner'' surface, e.g. a sheet of paper. This will hopefully eliminate dust problems, and yellow shadows.* Send it to DPC as the biggest 150 Kbyte JPEG file you can, not as a 60 Kbyte file. They re-compress the image, e.g. causing the texture of the cap to look like dust. Especially the thumbnail looks bad.* Watch the reflections e.g. in the bottle. Try maybe another sheet of paper.* Check the shadows under the bottle to get the shadow''s curve looking right.* Watch out for printed letters e.g. on the cap or the bottle.', '2004-10-16 18:01:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(962053, 110356, 24951, '<td valign="top">Oh what a beautiful shot. I gave you a ten. Nice to see your shots on this site (besides Treklens) You shoulda got 1st! People actually gave a 2! Give me a break!</td>', 'Oh what a beautiful shot. I gave you a ten. Nice to see your shots on this site (besides Treklens) You shoulda got 1st! People actually gave a 2! Give me a break!', '2004-10-16 22:25:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(962520, 110356, 714, '<td valign="top">Congrats, Brad!!!  Wonderful image of times gone by.</td>', 'Congrats, Brad!!!  Wonderful image of times gone by.', '2004-10-17 11:44:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(962650, 109200, 1934, '<td valign="top">bravó!</td>', 'bravó!', '2004-10-17 15:04:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(962825, 110116, 16301, '<td valign="top">Should have done better IMO...</td>', 'Should have done better IMO...', '2004-10-17 18:10:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(963119, 109956, 2158, '<td valign="top">As the challenge was ''parts'' I really didn''t think it mattered what it was.  I can''t believe it scored so poorly.</td>', 'As the challenge was ''parts'' I really didn''t think it mattered what it was.  I can''t believe it scored so poorly.', '2004-10-17 23:11:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(963277, 109956, 6349, '<td valign="top">I would have given this a 7 or an 8.  Very surprising score.</td>', 'I would have given this a 7 or an 8.  Very surprising score.', '2004-10-18 01:17:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(963817, 110331, 16266, '<td valign="top">Interesting image.  it looks like you burned the sky or did something selectivly to the sky, or tree as there is a visible line on the left most branch.  .. nice background and nice contrast between the branches and sky.  The framing is a little stale perhaps.. it is rather locked and doesn''t create tons of interest.  Perhaps up the constrast a bit.. the image is pretty middle grey everywhere...<br/>good start.<br/>-from the critique club.</td>', 'Interesting image.  it looks like you burned the sky or did something selectivly to the sky, or tree as there is a visible line on the left most branch.  .. nice background and nice contrast between the branches and sky.  The framing is a little stale perhaps.. it is rather locked and doesn''t create tons of interest.  Perhaps up the constrast a bit.. the image is pretty middle grey everywhere...good start.-from the critique club.', '2004-10-18 13:15:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(963821, 110440, 16266, '<td valign="top">good focus on the flower, and somewhat interesting photo.  I am not sure the hand adds to the picture or not.  It is blurry which brings out the flower, but it is still visible enough to know it is a hand.. and makes us think about it.. but not rellly intersting enough to keep our attention.  Perhaps if a bit of the child was in the background, or no hand, or something.  Good colors in the flower.<br/>-from the critique club.</td>', 'good focus on the flower, and somewhat interesting photo.  I am not sure the hand adds to the picture or not.  It is blurry which brings out the flower, but it is still visible enough to know it is a hand.. and makes us think about it.. but not rellly intersting enough to keep our attention.  Perhaps if a bit of the child was in the background, or no hand, or something.  Good colors in the flower.-from the critique club.', '2004-10-18 13:17:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(963822, 110175, 16266, '<td valign="top">looks like a lot of action.  All the people make an interesting composition.  it is very busy, which can be ok and the people make a nice sort of ''blank'' background, but the action in the image, which is perhaps the large flag, is very centered and in a ''boring'' position in the photo.  It is perhaps a little light, or too low contrast.  I don''t see any dark blacks... it is good to see the whole range of grey, from total white, to total black, with grey''s in the middle.. even if it is a high key (very white) or dark image... there should be a good tonal range.<br/> <br/>from the critique club.</td>', 'looks like a lot of action.  All the people make an interesting composition.  it is very busy, which can be ok and the people make a nice sort of ''blank'' background, but the action in the image, which is perhaps the large flag, is very centered and in a ''boring'' position in the photo.  It is perhaps a little light, or too low contrast.  I don''t see any dark blacks... it is good to see the whole range of grey, from total white, to total black, with grey''s in the middle.. even if it is a high key (very white) or dark image... there should be a good tonal range. from the critique club.', '2004-10-18 13:19:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(963825, 110447, 16266, '<td valign="top">nice detail and attention to parts.  it is not quite as sharp as i would like it.. perhaps a square framing would work better for this, i am not sure what bothers me about it.  Decent image.. good background color, perhaps a little boost of contrast would help this image a little.<br/>-from the critique club.</td>', 'nice detail and attention to parts.  it is not quite as sharp as i would like it.. perhaps a square framing would work better for this, i am not sure what bothers me about it.  Decent image.. good background color, perhaps a little boost of contrast would help this image a little.-from the critique club.', '2004-10-18 13:20:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(964211, 110323, 8860, '<td valign="top"><b>:: Hello from the Critique Club ::</b> <br/>............................................................<br/> <br/>Well, I''m sure you knew this wouldn''t win any awards - but your image does have character!<br/> <br/>It was a nice take on the challenge with good DOF and some effort made to use some directional light. Taking it seriously, I would offer the following by way of improvement:<br/>&gt; cleaner background<br/>&gt; get in even closer to lose more of the context<br/>&gt; a touch more lighting towards the front to pick up a bit more detail<br/> <br/>Hope this helps. : )<br/>Jon</td>', ':: Hello from the Critique Club :: ............................................................ Well, I''m sure you knew this wouldn''t win any awards - but your image does have character! It was a nice take on the challenge with good DOF and some effort made to use some directional light. Taking it seriously, I would offer the following by way of improvement:> cleaner background> get in even closer to lose more of the context> a touch more lighting towards the front to pick up a bit more detail Hope this helps. : )Jon', '2004-10-18 18:31:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(964230, 109428, 8860, '<td valign="top"><b>:: Hello from the Critique Club ::</b> <br/>............................................................<br/> <br/>This has been horribly under rated in my view.<br/> <br/>It has strong composition, it''s an imposing subject, it''s well lit and very striking. Why it rated so low truly astounds me.<br/> <br/>By way of critique I find it difficult to pick fault, but I just wonder whether cropping the bodywork on the left would make the image stronger?<br/> <br/>Don''t be put off by the result - this is good stuff.<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/>Jon</td>', ':: Hello from the Critique Club :: ............................................................ This has been horribly under rated in my view. It has strong composition, it''s an imposing subject, it''s well lit and very striking. Why it rated so low truly astounds me. By way of critique I find it difficult to pick fault, but I just wonder whether cropping the bodywork on the left would make the image stronger? Don''t be put off by the result - this is good stuff. CheersJon', '2004-10-18 18:41:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(964270, 110176, 8860, '<td valign="top"><b>:: Hello from the Critique Club ::</b> <br/>............................................................<br/> <br/>This shot is not as bad as its score indicates. You have interesting subject matter and some lovely motion from the water. But, from what I can gather, the voters would not have liked this for the following reasons:<br/>&gt; gloomy lighting which has left colour and contrast quite flat<br/>&gt; ''parts'' too obvious and unchallenging<br/>&gt; composition not engaging enough<br/> <br/>Improvements would be:<br/>&gt; better, brighter lighting<br/>&gt; less ''human'' viewpoint (eye-level is always a little dull)<br/>&gt; getting closer<br/> <br/>These are simple things to improve so I hope you don''t take poor ratings to heart, as this shows promise in my view.<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/>Jon</td>', ':: Hello from the Critique Club :: ............................................................ This shot is not as bad as its score indicates. You have interesting subject matter and some lovely motion from the water. But, from what I can gather, the voters would not have liked this for the following reasons:> gloomy lighting which has left colour and contrast quite flat> ''parts'' too obvious and unchallenging> composition not engaging enough Improvements would be:> better, brighter lighting> less ''human'' viewpoint (eye-level is always a little dull)> getting closer These are simple things to improve so I hope you don''t take poor ratings to heart, as this shows promise in my view. CheersJon', '2004-10-18 19:28:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(965625, 110378, 9964, '<td valign="top">amazing shot!</td>', 'amazing shot!', '2004-10-19 19:42:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(965631, 110367, 9964, '<td valign="top">great capture, fun image!</td>', 'great capture, fun image!', '2004-10-19 19:46:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(966886, 110176, 25024, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Imagineer:</b></div><hr/><i> <b>:: Hello from the Critique Club ::</b> <br/>............................................................<br/> <br/>This shot is not as bad as its score indicates. You have interesting subject matter and some lovely motion from the water. But, from what I can gather, the voters would not have liked this for the following reasons:<br/>&gt; gloomy lighting which has left colour and contrast quite flat<br/>&gt; ''parts'' too obvious and unchallenging<br/>&gt; composition not engaging enough<br/> <br/>Improvements would be:<br/>&gt; better, brighter lighting<br/>&gt; less ''human'' viewpoint (eye-level is always a little dull)<br/>&gt; getting closer<br/> <br/>These are simple things to improve so I hope you don''t take poor ratings to heart, as this shows promise in my view.<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/>Jon </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Many thanks Jon,<br/>I greatly appreciate your very constructive comments, all of which I agree with. This is the first critique I have received but it was well worth waiting for!. It is also made me feel better because this is the first entry that didn''t even merit one comment from anybody!<br/>Do you think I may have done better with the one I originally intended?<br/>Hmmm! I was going to attach my original image but it asks for a URL as opposed to my disk address. For my future reference and out of interest of your opinion, could you advise how I do that?</td>', 'Originally posted by Imagineer: :: Hello from the Critique Club :: ............................................................ This shot is not as bad as its score indicates. You have interesting subject matter and some lovely motion from the water. But, from what I can gather, the voters would not have liked this for the following reasons:> gloomy lighting which has left colour and contrast quite flat> ''parts'' too obvious and unchallenging> composition not engaging enough Improvements would be:> better, brighter lighting> less ''human'' viewpoint (eye-level is always a little dull)> getting closer These are simple things to improve so I hope you don''t take poor ratings to heart, as this shows promise in my view. CheersJon   Many thanks Jon,I greatly appreciate your very constructive comments, all of which I agree with. This is the first critique I have received but it was well worth waiting for!. It is also made me feel better because this is the first entry that didn''t even merit one comment from anybody!Do you think I may have done better with the one I originally intended?Hmmm! I was going to attach my original image but it asks for a URL as opposed to my disk address. For my future reference and out of interest of your opinion, could you advise how I do that?', '2004-10-20 13:58:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(967182, 110353, 21124, '<td valign="top">Original picture:<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=114344" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/21124/thumb/114344.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/21124/thumb/114344.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/21124/thumb/114344.jpg"/></a></td>', 'Original picture:', '2004-10-20 17:13:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(967742, 109813, 17203, '<td valign="top">I''m betting your score on this one suffered mostly from the lack of a clear subject. Focus, color and composition are fine, but there are four or five major elements competing for attention and the result is visual clutter. Worse, each of those elements is a ''whole'' thing in a Parts challenge. The high-scoring entries in this challenge all portrayed a section of one or two dominant objects. The compositions are simple, and I don''t think there was a ''whole'' object anywhere among the top 38 entries.</td>', 'I''m betting your score on this one suffered mostly from the lack of a clear subject. Focus, color and composition are fine, but there are four or five major elements competing for attention and the result is visual clutter. Worse, each of those elements is a ''whole'' thing in a Parts challenge. The high-scoring entries in this challenge all portrayed a section of one or two dominant objects. The compositions are simple, and I don''t think there was a ''whole'' object anywhere among the top 38 entries.', '2004-10-20 23:35:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(968432, 109428, 27293, '<td valign="top">This is awesome as it is. But, imo, it would have been even better if it was a horizontal shot with the orange light in the lower right golden section point or thereabout.<br/> <br/>Unfortunately, i didn''t get to vote on it for the parts challenge, it would have gotten a 10 from me.</td>', 'This is awesome as it is. But, imo, it would have been even better if it was a horizontal shot with the orange light in the lower right golden section point or thereabout. Unfortunately, i didn''t get to vote on it for the parts challenge, it would have gotten a 10 from me.', '2004-10-21 13:29:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(968501, 109428, 16004, '<td valign="top">i didn''t vote in this challenge, but i acknowledge your grief for it is a wonderful shot.  i love the angularity of it, and visually it''s very pleasing. only slight criticism is that the focus seems ever-so just a little bit too soft.  .  but that''s the ONLY quibble, and even that might be down to my eye sight as no one else has mentioned that.  this would not look out of place being framed and hanging on the wall of a diner.  hand on heart, i''d have given this a 8 or 9.</td>', 'i didn''t vote in this challenge, but i acknowledge your grief for it is a wonderful shot.  i love the angularity of it, and visually it''s very pleasing. only slight criticism is that the focus seems ever-so just a little bit too soft.  .  but that''s the ONLY quibble, and even that might be down to my eye sight as no one else has mentioned that.  this would not look out of place being framed and hanging on the wall of a diner.  hand on heart, i''d have given this a 8 or 9.', '2004-10-21 14:02:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(971443, 110131, 27293, '<td valign="top">This is absolutely marvelous! Would have gotten a 10 from me.</td>', 'This is absolutely marvelous! Would have gotten a 10 from me.', '2004-10-24 02:38:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(976537, 110359, 25742, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Artan:</b></div><hr/><i> I Like the composition and I thik the 2 tone was the right choise - but I would prefer the blacks to be darker.<br/> <br/>By th way my Arsenal play at Highbury and are currently top of the UK Football (that''s soccer to all you US citizens) Premier League </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>My first instinct was to have the blacks very dark, but then I lost the reflection of the 50mm on top of the 17-40, and I thought the reflection was quite nice.<br/>The white dots on the 17-40 are not scratches but lint and dust, give a nice worn feeling to the image IMHO. <br/> <br/>BTW your Arsenal just lost to Man City, after a long (49?) series without loss. That Rooney is a curse on Arsenal.</td>', 'Originally posted by Artan: I Like the composition and I thik the 2 tone was the right choise - but I would prefer the blacks to be darker. By th way my Arsenal play at Highbury and are currently top of the UK Football (that''s soccer to all you US citizens) Premier League   My first instinct was to have the blacks very dark, but then I lost the reflection of the 50mm on top of the 17-40, and I thought the reflection was quite nice.The white dots on the 17-40 are not scratches but lint and dust, give a nice worn feeling to the image IMHO.  BTW your Arsenal just lost to Man City, after a long (49?) series without loss. That Rooney is a curse on Arsenal.', '2004-10-27 15:56:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(977029, 109200, 16862, '<td valign="top">Það er rosaleg snilld að gera svona mynd við svona einfalt form</td>', 'Það er rosaleg snilld að gera svona mynd við svona einfalt form', '2004-10-27 21:10:36.000000', NULL, 0),
